# UI / UX

Reference: `docs/PROJECT_CONSTITUTION.md`, `docs/design/UI_GUIDELINES.md`

Pure UX. Do not prescribe colors, fonts, or visual tokens here.

## User first

Users must always know: where they are, what they are doing, what happens next, and whether the action succeeded.

## Cognitive load

- Present only what the current task needs.
- Hide advanced options until required.
- Cashiers work under time pressure — optimize for speed and low error rate.

## Page structure

```text
Header → Primary Actions → Summary → Main Content → Secondary Information
```

## Interaction

Every action needs immediate feedback: loading, success, failure, validation, disabled, empty.

## Consistency

Reuse existing interaction patterns. Do not invent a new pattern when one already exists.

## Design gate

A screen is ready only when the workflow is intuitive, hierarchy is obvious, and a first-time user can understand the page.
